diff --git a/rtl/formal/README.md b/rtl/formal/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8671c18
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# Formal proofs on the generated Verilog (L7)
+
+**Status: written, not yet run in the authoring environment.** `rtl/formal/` holds the property
+files and the job runner; the solver has not run here. `make formal` runs `run_formal.py`: for each
+hard-core block it injects `<block>.svh` in front of the final `endmodule` of `rtl/gen/<block>.v`
+(the checked-in Verilog is never edited), then runs SymbiYosys (`mode prove`, engine `smtbmc z3`): a
+bounded check, then k-induction, which is an unbounded proof when the induction closes.
+`make formal-<block>` runs one block; `make formal-equiv` runs only the netlist equivalence.
+
+`sby`, `yosys` and `z3` are in the program's container; a plain checkout has only `z3`. Where a job's
+tool is absent, `run_formal.py` prints `SKIP` for that job and still exits 0, with a banner saying
+no property was checked. **A `SKIP` is not a `PROVED`**: a green `make formal` in a tool-less checkout
+means "nothing was checked," and the properties are checked for real when `make formal` is run in the
+container. Outcomes print in four classes so a green run is never mistaken for a proof that did not
+run:
+
+    PROVED  <job>     a property held (a `prove` task)
+    GAP OK  <job>     a task marked `expect fail` found its counterexample: the RTL gap it documents
+                     is real. This is a finding, not a PASS.
+    SKIP    <job>     the tool the job needs is absent; it was not run
+    FAIL    <job>     a property that should hold was broken, or an expected counterexample was not found
+
+The first run in the container may need fixes to property syntax or induction strengthening; the
+outcomes below say what each job *asserts*, not what a run reported.
+
+Reset is assumed low (`assume(!rst)`): the properties are about operation, and a power loss is the
+high-water mark's job (`m_P8_hwm_floor`).
+
+## Property map
+
+P-numbers are those of `proofs/core_invariants.py` (the model-level theorems). A label marked
+**analogue** states the same *spirit* on the RTL but is not the model's statement verbatim -- the
+model's P6/P7/P13 are about "nothing executes while halted or heartbeat-lost," whereas the RTL blocks
+below are about the rung and the levers that *enforce* it. "CP" is the commit-point protocol
+(`proofs/commit_point.py`): of it the RTL holds only the hold (the rung does not leave HALT/SAFE
+without `clear`) and the binding of a clearance to its command (the mailbox's check order).
+
+| Block | Assertion prefix | P / CP | What it asserts |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `ticket_store` | `t_P3_*` | P3 | a burned id stays stored and unchanged; no duplicate ids; a burned id is always `seen` and never burns twice -- the id is a solver-chosen constant, so the claim is for every id; a full store refuses |
+| `epoch_reg` | `e_P9_*`, `e_P10_*` | P9, P10 (analogue) | the register changes only on `commit` with `quorum_ok`, then loads `new_epoch`; the host port has no effect. P10 here is an analogue: the block sees only `quorum_ok`, not the signature count |
+| `monotonic_counter` | `m_P8_*` | P8 | the value never decreases (the one exception is the 2^64 wrap, below); `load_hwm` raises it to at least the fuse mark; `dec_req` changes nothing |
+| `halt_seq` | `h_P5_*` | P5 | the rung never descends without `clear`; HALT and SAFE absorb; boot is the safe bottom with every lever held |
+| | `h_P6_*` | P6 (analogue) | RUN is entered only when armed (no cause, `hb_ok`, `loop_sense`); the loop switch closes only when armed, opens on tamper, loop loss and command halt, and `clear` does not close it |
+| | `h_P7_*`, `h_P13_*` | P7, P13 (analogue) | brake, reset, power and ports follow the rung exactly; every rung but RUN applies the brake and closes the ports -- the levers that keep nothing passing while halted |
+| `cap_table` | `c_P1_*` | P1, P4 | `allow` only against an entry that matches (point, peer, dir), is unexpired, has the current epoch tag and enough budget; an entry appears only by an insert with `mac_ok`; the budget never rises on lookup (no underflow) |
+| `mailbox` | `b_P3_*`, `b_P4_*`, `b_P12_*`, `b_P13_*`, `b_CP_*` | P3, P4, P12, P13, CP | dispatch only on a verified signature over the same command (`b_P12`); sequence above the slot's last (`b_P3`), epoch matched or exempt (`b_P4`); a `needs_run` command not dispatched while the rung is not RUN (`b_P13`, analogue); the checks run in order and the first failure is the status (`b_CP`); a wrong-command or bad-signature frame consumes nothing; the last-seq registers only rise. `b_P13` and the mailbox `b_P3`/`b_P12` default task lean on the front-end contract below |
+
+## Tasks that are expected to fail (findings about the RTL)
+
+Each is a `bmc` task with `expect fail`: the run prints `GAP OK` when the counterexample is found
+(that is the task succeeding -- the documented gap is real), and is not a `PASS`. They say which
+assumption the proofs lean on, and are the disproof of the three candidate RTL gaps.
+
+| Task | Finding |
+|---|---|
+| `monotonic_counter:wrap` | `inc` at 2^64-1 wraps to 0. Unreachable in practice (2^64 microseconds), but the block does not saturate. The `prove` task carries that one step as an escape clause, so P8 asserts as "never decreases except the wrap"; the `wrap` task asserts the strict form and is the counterexample (reached by loading a free `hwm` of 2^64-1, then incrementing -- two steps). A saturating increment would make P8 unconditional. |
+| `mailbox:nolatch` | The mailbox does not latch `frame_seq`, `key_slot` or `cmd` at the doorbell; it reads them live in VERIFY. If they change between doorbell and `sig_done`, a command dispatches with a sequence that is not above the last one (and `last_seq` can move backwards). The default `prove` task assumes the front end holds the frame while the mailbox is in VERIFY; `nolatch` drops that assumption and is the counterexample. Fix: latch the frame at the doorbell. |
+| `mailbox:midhalt` | `running` is checked only at the doorbell. If the rung leaves RUN during VERIFY, a `needs_run` command still dispatches. `midhalt` is the counterexample (a P13 analogue). Fix: re-check `running` at dispatch. |
+
+## Netlist equivalence
+
+`equiv:<block>` synthesizes `rtl/gen/<block>.v` with Yosys (`synth`, `abc -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX`) and proves it equivalent to the generated Verilog with `equiv_make`, `equiv_simple` and `equiv_induct` (sequential, matched registers, induction).
+
+This is an in-flow **Yosys** gate netlist, **not** the LibreLane netlist the brief names: `make gds`
+needs Docker and the PDK and no netlist from it is checked in, so the real comparison cannot run here.
+The Yosys check does prove the `abc`-mapped netlist equivalent to the generated Verilog, which is a
+meaningful gate-level equivalence for these blocks. Comparing the real `governor_core` netlist would
+need its standard-cell models; that job is not written.
diff --git a/rtl/formal/cap_table.svh b/rtl/formal/cap_table.svh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ade0cf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/cap_table.svh
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+// Formal properties for cap_table.
+// P1: nothing passes unless a rule allowed it: a lookup is allowed only against an entry with matching
+// (point, peer, dir), enough budget, not expired, and the current epoch tag. P4: the entry carries
+// the epoch (edition) tag, a stale tag is refused. The budget never underflows, and an entry is
+// inserted only with mac_ok.
+reg f_init = 1'b1;
+always @(posedge clk) f_init <= 1'b0;
+always @* assume (!rst);
+
+wire [7:0]   f_v  = {valid7, valid6, valid5, valid4, valid3, valid2, valid1, valid0};
+wire [191:0] f_bud = {budget7, budget6, budget5, budget4, budget3, budget2, budget1, budget0};
+wire [255:0] f_exp = {expiry7, expiry6, expiry5, expiry4, expiry3, expiry2, expiry1, expiry0};
+wire [127:0] f_tag = {etag7, etag6, etag5, etag4, etag3, etag2, etag1, etag0};
+wire [23:0]  f_pt  = {point7, point6, point5, point4, point3, point2, point1, point0};
+wire [127:0] f_peer = {peer7, peer6, peer5, peer4, peer3, peer2, peer1, peer0};
+wire [15:0]  f_dir = {dir7, dir6, dir5, dir4, dir3, dir2, dir1, dir0};
+
+reg [7:0]   p_v;
+reg [191:0] p_bud;
+reg p_ins, p_mac_ok, p_clear_all;
+always @(posedge clk) begin p_v <= f_v; p_bud <= f_bud; p_ins <= ins; p_mac_ok <= mac_ok; p_clear_all <= clear_all; end
+
+wire [7:0] f_ok;
+genvar gi;
+generate for (gi = 0; gi < 8; gi = gi + 1) begin : g_entry
+  assign f_ok[gi] = f_v[gi] && f_pt[gi*3 +: 3] == lk_point && f_peer[gi*16 +: 16] == lk_peer
+                    && (f_dir[gi*2 +: 2] == lk_dir || f_dir[gi*2 +: 2] == 2'd2)
+                    && f_exp[gi*32 +: 32] > now && f_tag[gi*16 +: 16] == epoch_tag
+                    && f_bud[gi*24 +: 24] >= lk_bytes;
+  always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init) begin
+    c_P1_budget_never_rises: assert (!p_v[gi] || f_bud[gi*24 +: 24] <= p_bud[gi*24 +: 24]);
+    c_P1_entry_appears_only_by_insert: assert (!(!p_v[gi] && f_v[gi]) || (p_ins && p_mac_ok && !p_clear_all));
+  end
+end endgenerate
+
+always @* begin
+  c_P1_allow_needs_a_matching_entry: assert (!allow || (lk && (|f_ok)));
+  c_P1_allow_reason_ok: assert (!allow || reason == 3'd0);
+  c_P1_insert_needs_mac: assert (!ins_ok || (ins && mac_ok));
+  c_P1_deny_has_a_reason: assert (allow || !lk || reason != 3'd0);
+end
diff --git a/rtl/formal/epoch_reg.svh b/rtl/formal/epoch_reg.svh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4b01058
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/epoch_reg.svh
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+// Formal properties for epoch_reg, injected before the final endmodule of rtl/gen/epoch_reg.v.
+// Numbers are the P-numbers of proofs/core_invariants.py (P9: an edition change needs a quorum;
+// P10, analogue: the block sees only the verifier's quorum_ok, not the signature count, so it asserts
+// the gate the count would open -- a change needs commit with quorum_ok).
+reg f_init = 1'b1;
+always @(posedge clk) f_init <= 1'b0;
+always @* assume (!rst);
+
+reg [255:0] p_epoch, p_new_epoch;
+reg p_commit, p_quorum_ok, p_host_wr;
+always @(posedge clk) begin
+  p_epoch <= epoch; p_new_epoch <= new_epoch;
+  p_commit <= commit; p_quorum_ok <= quorum_ok; p_host_wr <= host_wr;
+end
+
+always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init) begin
+  e_P9_change_needs_commit_and_quorum: assert (epoch == p_epoch || (p_commit && p_quorum_ok));
+  e_P9_commit_with_quorum_loads:       assert (!(p_commit && p_quorum_ok) || epoch == p_new_epoch);
+  e_P10_commit_without_quorum_no_op:   assert (!(p_commit && !p_quorum_ok) || epoch == p_epoch);
+  e_P9_host_write_has_no_effect:       assert (!(p_host_wr && !(p_commit && p_quorum_ok)) || epoch == p_epoch);
+end
+always @* begin
+  e_tag_is_low_16_bits: assert (epoch_tag == epoch[15:0]);
+  e_host_write_is_flagged: assert (host_refused == host_wr);
+end
diff --git a/rtl/formal/halt_seq.svh b/rtl/formal/halt_seq.svh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..79d968f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/halt_seq.svh
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+// Formal properties for halt_seq (the rung and the levers).
+// P5: halt is absorbing without an authorized clear, and boot is the safe bottom. P6 (analogue): the
+// model's "fail closed" is here "the rung reaches RUN only when armed." P7/P13 (analogue): the model's
+// "nothing executes while halted" is here enforced by the levers being applied in every rung but RUN,
+// so nothing passes while halted. The commit-point hold is the same register: the rung does not leave
+// HALT/SAFE except through `clear`, which the mailbox only raises on a signed CLEAR.
+localparam HI = 0, RUN = 1, THR = 2, HLT = 3, SAF = 4;
+localparam C_NONE = 0, C_LOOP = 1, C_LOCAL = 2, C_TAMPER = 3, C_COMMAND = 4;
+
+reg f_init = 1'b1;
+always @(posedge clk) f_init <= 1'b0;
+always @* assume (!rst);
+
+reg [2:0] p_state, p_cause;
+reg p_sw, p_clear, p_tamper, p_loop_lost, p_cmd_halt, p_hb_ok, p_loop_sense;
+always @(posedge clk) begin
+  p_state <= state; p_cause <= cause; p_sw <= switch_open;
+  p_clear <= clear; p_tamper <= tamper; p_loop_lost <= loop_lost; p_cmd_halt <= cmd_halt;
+  p_hb_ok <= hb_ok; p_loop_sense <= loop_sense;
+end
+
+wire p_in_run = (p_state == RUN) || (p_state == THR);
+wire p_cleared = p_clear && (p_state != HI);
+wire p_hard_cause = p_tamper || (p_loop_lost && p_in_run) || (p_cmd_halt && p_state != SAF);
+
+// invariants of the register state
+always @* begin
+  h_inv_state_in_range: assert (state <= SAF);
+  h_inv_cause_in_range: assert (cause <= C_COMMAND);
+  h_P6_inv_open_cause_keeps_switch_open: assert (!(cause == C_LOOP || cause == C_TAMPER || cause == C_COMMAND) || switch_open);
+  h_P6_inv_run_means_armed: assert (state != RUN || (cause == C_NONE && !switch_open));
+  h_P5_boot_safe_bottom: assert (!f_init || (state == HI && switch_open && cause == C_NONE && pwrbrk && perst && !pwr_en && ports_closed));
+  // levers follow the rung exactly, and every rung but RUN applies the brake and closes the ports
+  h_P7_pwrbrk:  assert (pwrbrk == (state != RUN));
+  h_P7_perst:   assert (perst == (state == HI || state == HLT || state == SAF));
+  h_P7_pwr_en:  assert (pwr_en == (state != HI && state != SAF));
+  h_P13_ports:  assert (ports_closed == (state != RUN));
+  h_P13_halted_means_levers: assert (!(state == HLT || state == SAF) || (pwrbrk && perst && ports_closed));
+end
+
+// transitions
+always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init) begin
+  h_P5_no_descent_without_clear: assert (state >= p_state || (p_cleared && state == HI && cause == C_NONE));
+  h_P5_halt_absorbing:  assert (!(p_state == HLT && !p_cleared) || (state == HLT || state == SAF));
+  h_P5_safe_absorbing:  assert (!(p_state == SAF && !p_cleared) || state == SAF);
+  h_P5_throttle_never_relaxes: assert (!(p_state == THR && !p_cleared) || state >= THR);
+  h_P6_enter_run_only_armed: assert (!(state == RUN && p_state != RUN) ||
+                                     (p_state == HI && p_cause == C_NONE && p_hb_ok && p_loop_sense && !p_tamper && !p_cmd_halt));
+  h_P6_hard_cause_opens_loop_and_halts: assert (!(p_hard_cause && !p_cleared) || (state >= HLT && switch_open));
+  h_P6_tamper_is_safe: assert (!(p_tamper && !p_cleared) || (state == SAF && cause == C_TAMPER && switch_open));
+  h_P6_switch_closes_only_armed: assert (!(p_sw && !switch_open) ||
+                                         (p_state == HI && p_cause == C_NONE && p_hb_ok && !p_tamper && !p_cmd_halt));
+  h_P6_clear_does_not_close_switch: assert (!p_cleared || (switch_open == p_sw && state == HI && cause == C_NONE));
+end
diff --git a/rtl/formal/mailbox.svh b/rtl/formal/mailbox.svh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0dd6bba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/mailbox.svh
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+// Formal properties for mailbox.
+// P3: no replay, the sequence must be above the slot's last accepted one, and last_seq only rises.
+// P4: the frame's epoch must match the epoch register or the command must be epoch-exempt. P12: a
+// command is dispatched only on a verified signature over that very command (a signature over a
+// heartbeat never dispatches CLEAR), and a failed check consumes nothing. P13 (analogue): a needs_run
+// command must not dispatch while the rung is not RUN. Commit point (CP): the checks run in order and
+// the first failure is what status reports.
+//
+// Interface assumption (default task): while the mailbox is in VERIFY, the frame fields it checked at the
+// doorbell are held (the RTL does not latch them). Tasks that drop an assumption are expected to
+// fail and document the gap:
+//   -D NOLATCH  frame_seq/key_slot/cmd may change during VERIFY: a dispatch with a stale sequence
+//   -D MIDHALT  `running` may fall during VERIFY: a needs_run command dispatches while not running
+reg f_init = 1'b1;
+always @(posedge clk) f_init <= 1'b0;
+always @* assume (!rst);
+
+wire [255:0] lseq = {seq7, seq6, seq5, seq4, seq3, seq2, seq1, seq0};
+wire [31:0] cur_last = lseq[key_slot*32 +: 32];
+wire seq_ok_now = frame_seq > cur_last;
+
+// what the frame looked like in the last cycle outside VERIFY, that is, at the doorbell
+reg [31:0] c_seq; reg [2:0] c_slot; reg [7:0] c_cmd; reg c_epm, c_epe;
+always @(posedge clk) if (!verify_req) begin
+  c_seq <= frame_seq; c_slot <= key_slot; c_cmd <= cmd; c_epm <= epoch_match; c_epe <= epoch_exempt;
+end
+`ifndef NOLATCH
+always @* if (verify_req) assume (frame_seq == c_seq && key_slot == c_slot && cmd == c_cmd
+                                  && epoch_match == c_epm && epoch_exempt == c_epe);
+`endif
+
+reg p_fsm, p_doorbell, p_sig_done, p_sig_ok, p_dispatch, p_seq_ok, p_epm, p_epe, p_nr, p_run;
+reg [31:0] p_seq; reg [2:0] p_slot; reg [7:0] p_cmd, p_signed; reg [255:0] p_lseq;
+always @(posedge clk) begin
+  p_fsm <= fsm_state; p_doorbell <= doorbell; p_sig_done <= sig_done; p_sig_ok <= sig_ok; p_dispatch <= dispatch;
+  p_seq_ok <= seq_ok_now; p_epm <= epoch_match; p_epe <= epoch_exempt; p_nr <= needs_run; p_run <= running;
+  p_seq <= frame_seq; p_slot <= key_slot; p_cmd <= cmd; p_signed <= signed_cmd; p_lseq <= lseq;
+end
+
+`ifdef NOLATCH
+always @* b_P3_dispatch_sequence_above_last: assert (!dispatch || seq_ok_now);
+`elsif MIDHALT
+// P13 (analogue): a needs_run command must not dispatch while the rung is not RUN. The RTL checks
+// running only at the doorbell, so a rung that leaves RUN during VERIFY is the counterexample.
+always @* b_P13_needs_run_rechecked_at_dispatch: assert (!dispatch || !needs_run || running);
+`else
+// P3 strengthening that makes the induction close: a frame in VERIFY passed the doorbell checks,
+// so its captured sequence is above the slot's last and its epoch matched or was exempt.
+always @* b_P3_inv_verify_passed_doorbell: assert (!fsm_state || (c_seq > lseq[c_slot*32 +: 32] && (c_epm || c_epe)));
+
+always @* begin
+  b_P12_dispatch_only_on_signed_same_command: assert (!dispatch || (verify_req && sig_done && sig_ok && signed_cmd == cmd));
+  b_P3_dispatch_sequence_above_last:          assert (!dispatch || seq_ok_now);
+  b_P4_dispatch_epoch_matches_or_exempt:      assert (!dispatch || epoch_match || epoch_exempt);
+  b_CP_no_dispatch_outside_verify:            assert (!dispatch || fsm_state);
+end
+
+genvar gi;
+generate for (gi = 0; gi < 8; gi = gi + 1) begin : g_slot
+  always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init)
+    b_P3_last_seq_only_rises: assert (lseq[gi*32 +: 32] >= p_lseq[gi*32 +: 32]);
+end endgenerate
+
+always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init) begin
+  b_P3_last_seq_changes_only_on_dispatch: assert (lseq == p_lseq || p_dispatch);
+  b_P3_dispatch_consumes_and_reports: assert (!p_dispatch || (status == 3'd2 && cmd_out == p_signed && cmd_out == p_cmd
+                                                          && lseq[p_slot*32 +: 32] == p_seq));
+  // the checks run in order and the first failure is what status reports (the commit-point protocol)
+  b_CP_order_sequence_first: assert (!(!p_fsm && p_doorbell && !p_seq_ok) || (status == 3'd4 && !fsm_state));
+  b_CP_order_epoch_second:   assert (!(!p_fsm && p_doorbell && p_seq_ok && !(p_epm || p_epe)) || (status == 3'd5 && !fsm_state));
+  b_CP_order_running_third:  assert (!(!p_fsm && p_doorbell && p_seq_ok && (p_epm || p_epe) && p_nr && !p_run) || (status == 3'd6 && !fsm_state));
+  b_CP_order_then_verify:    assert (!(!p_fsm && p_doorbell && p_seq_ok && (p_epm || p_epe) && !(p_nr && !p_run)) || (status == 3'd1 && fsm_state));
+  b_P12_wrong_command_consumes_nothing: assert (!(p_fsm && p_sig_done && p_sig_ok && p_signed != p_cmd) ||
+                                            (status == 3'd7 && lseq == p_lseq && !fsm_state));
+  b_P12_bad_signature_consumes_nothing: assert (!(p_fsm && p_sig_done && !p_sig_ok) || (status == 3'd3 && lseq == p_lseq && !fsm_state));
+end
+`endif
diff --git a/rtl/formal/monotonic_counter.svh b/rtl/formal/monotonic_counter.svh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8c360ac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/monotonic_counter.svh
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+// Formal properties for monotonic_counter. P8: the edition (here the time and anti-rollback
+// reference) only moves forward. Reset is assumed low: a power loss is the hwm's job (m_P8_hwm_floor).
+//
+// The register's only decreasing step is the wrap of an increment at 2^64-1 (2^64 microseconds,
+// about 584,000 years). The prove task carries that one step as an escape clause, so P8 holds
+// modulo it; the -D WRAP task asserts the strict form with no escape clause and is written to find
+// that step.
+//
+// The wrap is reached without fighting the register's init value (0): a free load_hwm strobe loads
+// the free input hwm -- the solver sets hwm = 2^64-1 -- and the following inc wraps it to 0. The
+// strict property is broken on that second step, at a depth of two. (An initial assume on value would
+// contradict the $initstate and leave no reachable trace, so the task would be vacuous; the load
+// path is the reachable way to 2^64-1.)
+reg f_init = 1'b1;
+always @(posedge clk) f_init <= 1'b0;
+always @* assume (!rst);
+
+reg [63:0] p_value, p_hwm;
+reg p_load, p_inc;
+always @(posedge clk) begin p_value <= value; p_hwm <= hwm; p_load <= load_hwm; p_inc <= inc; end
+
+always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init) begin
+`ifdef WRAP
+  m_P8_never_decreases_strict: assert (value >= p_value);
+`else
+  // the one exception is the wrap of an increment at 2^64-1 (2^64 microseconds, about 584,000 years)
+  m_P8_never_decreases: assert (value >= p_value || (p_inc && !p_load && p_value == 64'hFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF));
+  m_P8_hwm_floor:       assert (!p_load || (value >= p_hwm && value >= p_value));
+  m_P8_inc_by_one:      assert (!(p_inc && !p_load) || value == p_value + 64'd1);
+  m_P8_dec_req_no_effect: assert (p_load || p_inc || value == p_value);
+`endif
+end
+always @* m_P8_dec_refused_flag: assert (refused == dec_req);
diff --git a/rtl/formal/run_formal.py b/rtl/formal/run_formal.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7b23f2d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/run_formal.py
@@ -0,0 +1,193 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Formal jobs on the generated Verilog (rtl/gen/*.v). Used by ``make formal``.
+
+    python3 rtl/formal/run_formal.py            # every block, then the netlist equivalence
+    python3 rtl/formal/run_formal.py mailbox    # one block
+    python3 rtl/formal/run_formal.py equiv      # only the netlist equivalence
+
+For each block the properties in ``rtl/formal/<block>.svh`` are injected in front of the last
+``endmodule`` of the generated file (so they can read the block's registers; ``rtl/gen`` is never
+edited), and SymbiYosys runs ``mode prove`` (bounded model check, then k-induction: an unbounded
+proof when the induction closes).
+
+Outcomes are printed in four classes so a green ``make formal`` is never mistaken for a proof that
+did not run, and an expected counterexample is never mistaken for a pass:
+
+    PROVED  <job>     a property held (the ``prove`` task, ``mode prove``)
+    GAP OK  <job>     a task marked ``expect fail`` found its counterexample: the RTL gap it
+                     documents is real, and the task did its job. This is not a PASS.
+    SKIP    <job>     the tool the job needs is not on PATH; it was not run. Skips do not fail
+                     the command, but a SKIP is not a PROVED -- it says nothing was checked.
+    FAIL    <job>     a property that should hold was broken, or an expected counterexample was
+                     not found (the documented gap was not reproduced).
+
+The program's container has ``sby``, ``yosys`` and ``z3``; where they are absent (as in a plain
+checkout) the jobs are skipped and the command still exits 0, with a banner saying so -- the
+properties are checked for real when the command is run in the container.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+import sys
+
+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
+GEN = os.path.join(HERE, "..", "gen")
+BUILD = os.path.join(HERE, "build")
+
+# block -> tasks: name -> (mode, depth, defines, expected).
+# expected is "pass" for a property that must hold, "fail" for a task that documents an RTL gap and
+# is written to produce the counterexample (SymbiYosys ``expect fail``).
+BLOCKS = {
+    "ticket_store": {"prove": ("prove", 6, [], "pass")},
+    "epoch_reg": {"prove": ("prove", 4, [], "pass")},
+    "halt_seq": {"prove": ("prove", 8, [], "pass")},
+    "cap_table": {"prove": ("prove", 5, [], "pass")},
+    "monotonic_counter": {"prove": ("prove", 4, [], "pass"), "wrap": ("bmc", 3, ["WRAP"], "fail")},
+    "mailbox": {"prove": ("prove", 8, [], "pass"),
+                "nolatch": ("bmc", 6, ["NOLATCH"], "fail"),
+                "midhalt": ("bmc", 6, ["MIDHALT"], "fail")},
+}
+# blocks whose gate-level netlist is compared with the generated Verilog
+EQUIV = ["ticket_store", "epoch_reg", "halt_seq", "cap_table", "monotonic_counter", "mailbox"]
+
+# tools each kind of job needs; smtbmc z3 runs under sby, the equivalence runs under yosys
+NEEDS_BLOCK = ("sby", "z3")
+NEEDS_EQUIV = ("yosys",)
+
+
+def inject(block: str, dest: str) -> None:
+    with open(os.path.join(GEN, block + ".v")) as f:
+        lines = f.read().splitlines()
+    with open(os.path.join(HERE, block + ".svh")) as f:
+        props = f.read()
+    last = max(i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith("endmodule"))
+    out = lines[:last] + ["// ---- injected by rtl/formal/run_formal.py ----", props] + lines[last:]
+    with open(dest, "w") as f:
+        f.write("\n".join(out) + "\n")
+
+
+def _tail(p: subprocess.CompletedProcess) -> str:
+    return "\n".join((p.stdout + p.stderr).strip().splitlines()[-12:])
+
+
+def run_block(block: str, missing: list[str]) -> list[tuple[str, str, str]]:
+    tasks = BLOCKS[block]
+    if any(t in missing for t in NEEDS_BLOCK):
+        return [(f"{block}:{t}", "skip", f"{', '.join(t for t in NEEDS_BLOCK if t in missing)} not on PATH; not run")
+                for t in tasks]
+    d = os.path.join(BUILD, block)
+    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
+    inject(block, os.path.join(d, block + ".v"))
+    sby = ["[tasks]"] + list(tasks) + ["", "[options]"]
+    for t, (mode, depth, _defs, expected) in tasks.items():
+        sby += [f"{t}: mode {mode}", f"{t}: depth {depth}"]
+        if expected == "fail":
+            sby.append(f"{t}: expect fail")
+    sby += ["", "[engines]", "smtbmc z3", "", "[script]"]
+    for t, (_m, _d, defs, _e) in tasks.items():
+        flags = "".join(f" -D {x}" for x in defs)
+        sby.append(f"{t}: read_verilog -formal -sv{flags} {block}.v")
+    sby += [f"prep -top {block}", "", "[files]", f"{block}.v", ""]
+    with open(os.path.join(d, block + ".sby"), "w") as f:
+        f.write("\n".join(sby))
+    results = []
+    for t, (_m, _d, _defs, expected) in tasks.items():
+        p = subprocess.run(["sby", "-f", f"{block}.sby", t], cwd=d, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=3000)
+        held = p.returncode == 0
+        if expected == "fail":
+            # the task is written to find the counterexample; a clean run means the gap is real
+            status = "gap" if held else "fail"
+            note = ("expected counterexample found: " + _tail(p).splitlines()[-1]
+                    if held else
+                    "expected counterexample not found -- the documented gap was not reproduced")
+        else:
+            status = "proved" if held else "fail"
+            note = "" if held else _tail(p)
+        results.append((f"{block}:{t}", status, note))
+    return results
+
+
+def run_equiv(block: str, missing: list[str]) -> tuple[str, str, str]:
+    """rtl/gen/<block>.v against the same design synthesized to a gate netlist (yosys synth + abc).
+
+    This is the in-flow Yosys gate netlist, not the LibreLane netlist: ``make gds`` needs Docker
+    and the PDK and no netlist from it is checked in. It proves the abc-mapped netlist is equivalent
+    to the generated Verilog; comparing the real ``governor_core`` netlist would need its cell models.
+    """
+    if any(t in missing for t in NEEDS_EQUIV):
+        return (f"equiv:{block}", "skip", f"{', '.join(missing)} not on PATH; not run")
+    d = os.path.join(BUILD, "equiv")
+    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
+    src = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(GEN, block + ".v"))
+    script = f"""
+read_verilog -sv {src}
+hierarchy -top {block}
+proc
+flatten
+dffunmap
+opt_clean
+design -stash gold
+read_verilog -sv {src}
+hierarchy -top {block}
+synth -flatten -top {block}
+dffunmap
+abc -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX
+opt_clean
+tee -o {block}.gates.stat stat
+write_verilog -noattr {block}.gates.v
+design -stash gate
+design -copy-from gold -as gold {block}
+design -copy-from gate -as gate {block}
+equiv_make gold gate equiv
+hierarchy -top equiv
+equiv_simple -seq 5
+equiv_induct -seq 5
+equiv_status -assert
+"""
+    path = os.path.join(d, block + ".ys")
+    with open(path, "w") as f:
+        f.write(script)
+    p = subprocess.run(["yosys", "-q", "-l", block + ".log", block + ".ys"], cwd=d, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=3000)
+    held = p.returncode == 0
+    return (f"equiv:{block}",
+            "proved" if held else "fail",
+            "" if held else _tail(p))
+
+
+def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
+    missing = [t for t in ("sby", "yosys", "z3") if shutil.which(t) is None]
+    if missing:
+        print(f"SKIP    tooling absent: {', '.join(missing)} not on PATH "
+              f"(the program's container has sby/yosys-smtbmc/z3). No property was checked; "
+              f"run `make formal` in the container to run them.")
+    want = argv or list(BLOCKS) + ["equiv"]
+    results: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = []
+    for w in want:
+        if w == "equiv":
+            results += [run_equiv(b, missing) for b in EQUIV]
+        elif w in BLOCKS:
+            results += run_block(w, missing)
+        else:
+            print(f"unknown job {w}")
+            return 2
+    labels = {"proved": "PROVED  ", "gap": "GAP OK  ", "skip": "SKIP    ", "fail": "FAIL    "}
+    for name, status, note in results:
+        line = labels[status] + name
+        if status in ("gap", "fail") and note:
+            line += "  " + " ".join(note.split())
+        print(line)
+    for name, status, note in results:
+        if status == "fail" and note:
+            print("      " + note.replace("\n", "\n      "))
+    fails = [r for r in results if r[1] == "fail"]
+    skipped = sum(1 for r in results if r[1] == "skip")
+    if skipped:
+        print(f"SKIP    {skipped} job(s) not run (tools absent). A SKIP is not a PROVED; "
+              f"run in the container to check the properties.")
+    return 0 if not fails else 1
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
diff --git a/rtl/formal/ticket_store.svh b/rtl/formal/ticket_store.svh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f8f96b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtl/formal/ticket_store.svh
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+// Formal properties for ticket_store. P3: no replay, a burned id is never admitted again.
+reg f_init = 1'b1;
+always @(posedge clk) f_init <= 1'b0;
+always @* assume (!rst);
+
+wire [7:0]   f_v  = {v7, v6, v5, v4, v3, v2, v1, v0};
+wire [255:0] f_id = {id7, id6, id5, id4, id3, id2, id1, id0};
+reg  [7:0]   p_v;
+reg  [255:0] p_id;
+always @(posedge clk) begin p_v <= f_v; p_id <= f_id; end
+
+// a witness id chosen by the solver and held fixed: the claim is for every id
+(* anyconst *) wire [31:0] w_id;
+reg w_burned = 1'b0;
+always @(posedge clk) if (burned && id_in == w_id) w_burned <= 1'b1;
+
+wire [7:0] w_hit;
+genvar gi, gj;
+generate for (gi = 0; gi < 8; gi = gi + 1) begin : g_entry
+  assign w_hit[gi] = f_v[gi] && f_id[gi*32 +: 32] == w_id;
+  always @(posedge clk) if (!f_init) begin
+    t_P3_valid_never_clears: assert (!p_v[gi] || f_v[gi]);
+    t_P3_burned_id_never_changes: assert (!p_v[gi] || f_id[gi*32 +: 32] == p_id[gi*32 +: 32]);
+  end
+  for (gj = gi + 1; gj < 8; gj = gj + 1) begin : g_pair
+    always @* t_P3_no_duplicate_ids: assert (!(f_v[gi] && f_v[gj]) || f_id[gi*32 +: 32] != f_id[gj*32 +: 32]);
+  end
+end endgenerate
+
+always @* begin
+  t_P3_burn_only_of_unseen_id: assert (!burned || !seen);
+  t_P3_full_refuses_burn:      assert (!(burned && full));
+  t_P3_full_means_all_valid:   assert (full == (&f_v));
+  t_P3_burned_id_is_seen:      assert (!(w_burned && id_in == w_id) || seen);
+  t_P3_burned_id_is_stored:    assert (!w_burned || (|w_hit));
+  t_P3_no_second_burn:         assert (!(w_burned && id_in == w_id) || !burned);
+end
